# Settings for this patient device. Copy it and edit your copy:
#   cp apps/patient-desktop/.env.example apps/patient-desktop/.env
# .env is gitignored - never commit it. A real environment variable overrides the .env file.

# --- Which patient this device belongs to ---
# The pseudonymous Patient.id (= patients.id in Supabase). NOT a bed label: beds are display-only
# and get reused. Every action the assistant takes (item requests, nurse calls, emergencies) is
# recorded for this patient.
#
# Demo ward patients (server/sim/vitals_sim.py DEMO_WARD, beds 4W-01..05):
#   8398b128-7c86-69f2-456a-a0afb52067c1   4W-01  80-89 M
#   5a4445ed-e27a-6c4c-96bd-307b7bbee226   4W-02  80-89 F  (sepsis scenario)
#   9020f065-b607-4ea6-719f-2ea65bb06c8b   4W-03  70-79 M
#   1ebf325c-5fd9-9259-79cf-44f209b97ee8   4W-04  60-69 F  (loose SpO2 probe)
#   94011f7c-9aaa-e26e-a4e8-fe735f840734   4W-05  60-69 M
PATIENT_ID=

# --- Where the assistant's requests go ---
# Each action is POSTed to the vitals simulator server (server/sim/cli.py), which writes it to the
# Supabase `alerts` table for the nurse dashboard. Only the patient id and fixed categories are sent
# (e.g. nurse_call / pain / soon), never what the patient said. Leave either value empty to only log
# requests in this terminal.
#
# The simulator's URL: the Render service (https://<service>.onrender.com), or http://127.0.0.1:8765
# for `pnpm sim:serve` on this machine.
SIM_URL=
# Must equal PATIENT_REQUEST_TOKEN on the simulator (Render: vitals-simulator -> Environment; locally:
# the repo-root .env). It only lets this device send patient requests. The demo-control token
# (SIM_CONTROL_TOKEN) is a different secret and never goes on a patient device.
PATIENT_REQUEST_TOKEN=
